+## `esp32-2432s022-spi` — the ESP32-2432S022C, its panel on SPI (classic ESP32)
+
+A stand-in for the ESP32-2432S022C (2.2" ST7789 240×320, CST820 touch) for firmware built with an SPI panel back end:
+the board drives its panel over an 8-bit i80 bus (I2S0 in LCD mode), which is not modelled.
+
+| Device | Bus | Model |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| ST7789 240×320 panel | the T-Display's SPI wiring above | `DcsPanel::st7789()`; the glass is the whole GRAM |
+| CST820 touch | I2C0 at 0x15, SDA 21 / SCL 22 | `Cst820`: 0x02 finger count, 0x03..0x06 X and Y; `touch X Y 1\|0` in a script, the board UI's pointer |
+| Backlight, buttons | as the T-Display | |
+
 ## `none` — bare module
 
 No devices; console only. For stock ESP-IDF projects (`examples/hello_world`).
